  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Mocha Response - Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tropical Cyclone Mocha made landfall near Sittwe in Myanmar on the afternoon of 14 May 2023, with widespread impacts across the coast in Myanmar and Bangladesh. According to estimates by the United Nations (UN), 2.3 million people live in the affected areas in Bangladesh. This includes 1.3 million Bangladesh nationals, as well as 960,000
Rohingya refugees who are already entirely dependant on humanitarian assistance.
The cyclone Mocha investment&apos;s objective is to provide post-cyclone support to affected populations, predominantly cyclone-affected Bangladeshi communities. Our assistance supported humanitarian partners to reconstruct and repair houses and community structures, provide cash support to cyclone-affected people, distribution of essential household items, and pre-positioning and capacity building to withstand future disasters or adverse weather events. The total estimated investment value is AUD 2.5m over 8 months, from May - December 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
